<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@/~part_IV__cl_9__subsec_1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0#subsection> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@/~part_IV__cl_9__subsec_1> <https://schema.org/text> "If an accused reasonably expects to disclose or to cause the disclosure of sensitive information in any manner, in his defence, the accused shall give two days’ notice to the Public Prosecutor and the court in writing of his intention to do so."@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@/~part_IV__cl_9__subsec_2> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#is_part_of> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@/~part_IV__cl_9> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@> .
