<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@/~part_VII__cl_18> <https://schema.org/text> "A statement made, whether orally or in writing, in the course of, or for the purposes of, an investigation or inquiry into a security offence by any person who is dead or who cannot be found, or who has become incapable of giving evidence shall be admissible as evidence. Conviction based on testimony of a child of tender years"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@/~part_VII__cl_19> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#is_part_of> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@/~part_VII> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/15/eng@> .
